# Designing Tinder for an SDE-2 System Design Interview

A strong Tinder system design answer should focus on:

* Geospatial matching
* Recommendation engine
* Real-time interactions
* High write throughput
* Feed ranking
* Scalability
* Low latency
* Privacy and abuse prevention

The interviewer mainly wants to evaluate:

* Distributed systems understanding
* Feed/recommendation architecture
* Real-time event handling
* Database design decisions
* Scalability tradeoffs

---

# 1. Clarify Requirements

Start by asking clarifying questions.

## Functional Requirements

Users should be able to:

* Create profile
* Upload photos
* Set preferences
* Discover nearby users
* Swipe left/right
* Match when both like each other
* Chat after matching
* Receive notifications

Optional:

* Boosts
* Super Likes
* Premium subscriptions
* Rewind

---

## Non-Functional Requirements

* Low latency feed loading
* High availability
* Massive scalability
* Real-time matching
* Geo-aware search
* Fault tolerance
* Abuse/spam prevention

---

# 2. Scale Estimation

Example assumptions:

* 100M DAU
* 10M concurrent users
* Billions of swipes/day
* Millions of matches/day

Important insight:

> Tinder is write-heavy because every swipe is an event.

This is a good interview point.

